    {
      "id": "claim_e5ed1cf70cd24702979c9bed7c93b805",
      "statement": "Because a branch-protection required-check glob like `guardrails*` or `app-ci / app-e2e*` matches a context regardless of its event suffix, ci-status.mjs separates the whole-commit verdict (which evaluates every context any required glob matches, across all events, the same way branch protection does) from the single-event view chosen by --pr/--event; a verdict that only looked at one event previously reported VERDICT mergeable for a commit whose required context had actually failed on a different event, and the subsequent merge call was rejected by the forge.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/ci-status.mjs#L214-L263",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ffc7221a059b53cb2f4ea5a70dd3e3cdde866e6ca7f17c39c64a621190b74579:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_542d808cc2d2444ba521542e36ac7a7a",
      "statement": "bundleJobName() in ci-status.mjs must derive the evidence-bundle-owning job differently depending on context shape: a real Actions check renders as `<workflow> / <job>` with spaces, where the job is the trailing segment, while a job's self-posted narrow status such as `infra-image-scan/weekly` carries no ` / ` separator and the bundle-owning job is the leading segment, not the trailing label; using tail-splitting uniformly on the narrow form produces a confident false '404, bundle not found' for a bundle that exists under the correct name.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://scripts/ci-status.mjs#L220-L249",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b707b9e8cae36cf3212ab623e2dd99f70e6408c506aed181c9093aea29405e82:"
        }
      ]
