    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea57244cc0c24e9986b8e3114b133d3b",
      "statement": "A pull request opened via an AGit push (HEAD:refs/for/main) has no backing branch, so Forgejo treats the run as untrusted and executes it without Actions secrets, silently emptying every ${{ secrets.* }} rather than failing the job outright; ci-status.mjs detects and prints a DETACHED HEAD warning for this case because the resulting failure (e.g. a rejected remote-cache request) otherwise looks like an unrelated credential or infrastructure fault.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/runbooks/ci-diagnostics.md#L935-L959",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:590696c7049e250734122d05d310edb6703e894edc6b6ff72a458c1caee5abc7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4d81acfe57ce4859961b053bdf91cf81",
      "statement": "mc-service writes its domain-event log line at the end of a request handler, in the same emit as the response, so logs/mc-service.log's line order is completion order rather than start order: logging_middleware awaits next.run(request) and only then emits the `request completed` event carrying a numeric duration_ms, and handlers such as create_collection/delete_collection log their domain event after the command returns. Reconstructing true temporal (start) order for a bundle's mc-service log therefore requires subtracting each line's own duration_ms from its timestamp and sorting on that rather than trusting file order, and a cross-worker race hypothesis built from adjacent raw lines can be entirely inverted by this (item #568).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://backend/mc-service/src/api/collections/create.rs#L17-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ad745677efef37417fc301ce0fafe08d3b75984df5725c8416c26cb2f6f236eb:"
        },
