    {
      "id": "claim_6b0034cc42ba41a59fa8ae2038063ba2",
      "statement": "Cross-worker or cross-actor race hypotheses drawn from mc-service.log should be checked against `subject` / `preferred_username` / `authorized_party` before being accepted: authorized_party separates the actors even when every E2E worker acts as the same subject (movie-collection-manager = browser/BFF session, agent-gateway = the agent's downscoped write token) and preferred_username names the worker, while mc-service scopes collections by owner_id = token.subject in every collection endpoint, so two lines with different subject values cannot be acting on the same collection and a foreign worker's delete is impossible rather than a race to narrow.",
